x86_64-linux  Box's constructor belongs to a class template, and clang emits only the C2 variant of a specialization's constructor on this target whether it is written inside the class or outside it (template-out-of-line-constructor measures the second) where cxx1 emits C1 and C2 - the difference move-constructor.nonames records. arm64-darwin and x86_64-windows agree name for name.
